# siege-gap: an army on ONE attack-move order must pass a gap two cells wide in a wall, and an enemy body (hp 9,000,
# unarmed) stands in the gap. The bodies with a line to it get an attack ahead of their leg and stand firing; the
# other fifty wait behind that firing line for some 6,000 ticks. When the target dies the order goes on through the
# gap to the click 50 cells beyond.
# A body that combat holds in reach from the first tick of its attack never asks for a route, so it has no Legion
# member; the stand-down read such a body as dead since its last step and ended the orders of the bodies waiting
# behind it after 4,800 ticks, and of the bodies behind those 600 ticks later (43, 23, 49 and 56 of 60 arrived at
# offsets 0, 1, -1, -2; all 60 without the rule). A body on an attack or guard leg is its owner's to end, with a
# member or without: the firing line is live, and so is everything queued behind it.
# At start offsets 2..5 fewer bodies find a line to the target, it outlives the run, and the whole army waits to
# tick 14,000 with its orders (51 to 58 of the 60 were ended).
# No baselined fixture with weapons on runs past tick 5,400; this one runs the long stand-down under fire.
# Keys: g.A.arrived (60 at offsets 0, 1, -1, -2), scale.complete_outside_n (0 at every offset: no order ends off the
# arrival disc), work.stand_downs.total (absent: none).
scn 1
name siege-gap
ticks 14000
seed 7
players 2
team 0 0
team 1 1
wanderers off
map flat 220 160
wall 128 0 4 79
wall 128 81 4 79
type a mover 1 2500 10 1.8 gun=96,1,1.0
type tgt mover 2 2500 10 1.8 hp=9000
group A 0 a 60 rect 20 74 40 86 pitch=2 weapons=on
group T 1 tgt 1 cells 128,79 weapons=off
reach ring A T marks=1200,2400
at 1 fight A 180 80
